<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">A-Group culture</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 3800 – c. 2900 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The A-Group culture flourished in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-nubia">Lower Nubia</a>, between the First and Second Cataracts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a>, from about 3800 BCE. Its people farmed, herded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> and traded with Predynastic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, and they made fine thin-walled painted pottery. Rich tombs at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qustul">Qustul</a> suggest a ruling elite. The culture disappears from the record after Egyptian campaigns in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/early-dynastic-period">Early Dynastic period</a>.</p></div>
